      <section class="section shell" id="approach">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2>Clear thinking. Practical outcomes.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="approach-grid">
          <div class="approach-copy">
            <p class="lead">
              Good security engineering is not a gate at the end of delivery. It
              is a set of well-designed decisions that help a team move with
              confidence.
            </p>
            <p>
              I work from threat models and real operational constraints, then
              turn them into controls people can understand, automate, and
              improve. The goal is a safer system and a stronger engineering
              culture.
            </p>
          </div>
          <ol class="principles" role="list">
            <li class="principle">
              <h3>Understand the system</h3>
              <p>
                Map assets, identities, data flows, and the risks that matter to
                the business.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li class="principle">
              <h3>Reduce the blast radius</h3>
              <p>
                Prefer small, composable controls over brittle security theatre.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li class="principle">
              <h3>Make the secure path easy</h3>
              <p>
                Build feedback loops and defaults that work with the team, not
                against it.
              </p>
